<article class="env-lemma" id="08DS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08DS">Lemma <span data-tag="08DS">30.26.10</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a locally Noetherian scheme. Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes which is locally of finite type. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module with support proper over $S$. Then $R^ pf_*\mathcal{F}$ is a coherent $\mathcal{O}_ S$-module for all $p \geq 0$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/0CYS" data-tag="0CYS">30.26.7</a> there exists a closed immersion $i : Z \to X$ and a finite type, quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ Z$-module $\mathcal{G}$ such that (a) $g = f \circ i : Z \to S$ is proper, and (b) $i_*\mathcal{G} = \mathcal{F}$. We see that $R^ pg_*\mathcal{G}$ is coherent on $S$ by Proposition <a href="/tag/02O5" data-tag="02O5">30.19.1</a>. On the other hand, $R^ qi_*\mathcal{G} = 0$ for $q > 0$ (Lemma <a href="/tag/01Y6" data-tag="01Y6">30.9.9</a>). By Cohomology, Lemma <a href="/tag/01F6" data-tag="01F6">20.13.8</a> we get $R^ pf_*\mathcal{F} = R^ pg_*\mathcal{G}$ which concludes the proof. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>